PAIR_POSE_PRESERVATION_POLICY = "PAIR STANDING-POSE LOCK — HIGHEST PRIORITY: Image 1 supplies each person's identity, anatomy, clothes, belongings and contact, never the output scenery. Regardless of source posture or global photo rotation, render both fully upright and standing: vertical necks and torsos, level shoulders and pelvis, straight neutral spines and natural leg alignment. Seated/reclining/lying or cropped bodies are completed as standing anatomy; portrait canvas orientation is not a pose instruction. Do not invent torso bends or copy a diagonally rotated whole person. HEAD TILT DEFAULT — EXACTLY 0 DEGREES: Head centered above its own neck, crown directly above chin/nose, eye line horizontal, both ears level. Never cock, cant, slant or tilt a head toward the other person. Keep proven yaw/gaze independent of roll. Identity crops provide face/hair only: ignore their apparent head angle, and reconstruct the head upright. When converting posture to standing, discard the source head-to-image angle and align the head to the reconstructed vertical neck. Source frame angle, diagonal body, gaze, hairstyle, face/crop tilt alone never proves local tilt. Only a facial midline clearly angled relative to BOTH the same person's neck AND continuous upright torso after common rotation removal permits roll; if either axis is unclear, keep 0 degrees."

PAIR_RECONSTRUCTION_TARGET_POLICY = "PAIR RECONSTRUCTION TARGET: Rebuild exactly the two face-anchored people as complete 3D cartoon figures. Always render both upright and standing, regardless of source posture, with vertical necks and torsos, level shoulders and pelvis, straight neutral spines, heads centered above necks, and natural leg alignment. Complete unseen regions as standing anatomy. For a source-separated pair, choose contact after preserving each existing hand action; use a eligible source-unposed arm or direct body contact; keep both heads level, torsos straight and legs in a natural standing stance. Preserve clear gaze, facial direction and held objects. Head roll is exactly 0 degrees unless unmistakable same-person facial-midline evidence differs from both the neck axis and continuous torso axis after shared camera rotation is removed; if uncertain, keep 0 degrees."

PAIR_HUMAN_ONLY_POLICY = "HUMAN-ONLY PAIR OUTPUT: Render exactly the two face-anchored people; remove animals and all other people. Render both people standing upright regardless of source posture, with straight neutral torsos and level heads. Preserve visible inanimate belongings and each person's owned hand/object actions."

PAIR_FINAL_POSE_AUDIT = "FINAL PAIR POSE AUDIT — APPLY LAST: If converting a reclining or diagonally framed source person to standing, discard source head-to-image roll and align the head to the reconstructed vertical neck. A tilted source face or identity crop alone is never proof of local head tilt; only distinct same-person head-versus-neck-versus-continuous-torso axes can justify nonzero roll. Remove shared camera/photo roll. Render both people standing upright, with vertical necks and torsos, level shoulders and pelvis, straight neutral spines, heads centered above their necks, crowns directly above chins, noses centered over necks, eye lines horizontal, both ears level, and natural leg alignment, regardless of source pose. Do not cock, cant, slant or tilt a head toward the other person; head yaw/gaze may turn while roll remains zero. Every final person must stand upright in a natural neutral stance, regardless of whether the source shows sitting, crouching, reclining or lying. Keep both torsos vertical and straight and both heads level; never transfer global camera roll into the body or head. Fill cropped parts consistently with standing anatomy. For a separated pair only, an optional hand connector may minimally repose one eligible source-unposed existing arm; direct body contact needs no connecting hand; keep torsos straight, heads level and legs in natural standing alignment. Head roll remains exactly 0 degrees unless unmistakable same-person head-versus-neck-versus-continuous-torso evidence proves local tilt; if uncertain, keep 0 degrees. Do not copy a globally rotated photo as a diagonal figure; remove camera roll and retain natural upright standing alignment."

PAIR_FINAL_STYLE_POLICY = "FINAL PAIR STYLE CHECK: Exactly two distinct, complete, non-photorealistic sculpted cartoon figures in one continuous portrait 2:3 composition on a clean solid white seamless background. Remove all source scenery, walls, doors, signs, furniture, objects and environmental detail; retain only the two people and soft contact shadows. Show each person head-to-feet in a natural upright standing pose. Keep a straight neutral torso, level head and naturally aligned legs; do not add a fashion lean, torso bend or head tilt without clear same-person evidence. Keep proportions along each person’s body axis, use one shared support/floor plane appropriate to that posture, and add soft contact shadows without any display base. Keep identities, clothes, objects and limbs separately owned."

PAIR_HUMAN_OUTPUT_TEMPLATE_POLICY = 'FINAL PAIR OUTPUT TEMPLATE — AFTER IDENTITY ANCHORS: Return exactly two complete distinct cartoon figures standing on a clean solid white seamless background with no scenery and no display base. Apply the standing/head evidence rules above: vertical straight torsos, neutral spine, level shoulders/pelvis and natural legs; complete seated/reclining/lying/cropped sources as standing anatomy. Head roll stays exactly 0 degrees unless Image 1 proves the full same-person head-versus-neck-versus-continuous-torso comparison; if uncertain, keep 0 degrees. Keep proven yaw/gaze independently. Anchors provide face/hair identity only, never pose or scale; never copy their apparent head angle or transfer anchor crop roll into the final head. Enforce the stated 24–26% complete head/crown scale for each person. Preserve reasonable contact only between the two anchored people under CONTACT ELIGIBILITY. Keep visible hand poses, sides, grips, belongings and clothing ownership. New hand contact may use only a source-unposed arm with no conflicting supported action, replacing its former position. Otherwise use shoulder/upper-arm/elbow/torso surfaces without a new grasp. Gender alone does not imply romance; adult-child contact is protective. Keep the four arms readable under the final arm audit. Return one image.'

NO_ADDED_DISPLAY_BASE_RULE = 'NO ADDED DISPLAY BASE — ABSOLUTE: Render the complete subject(s) directly on the continuous white seamless studio floor, with only a soft contact/floor shadow. Weight-bearing shoe soles, feet or paws contact that floor directly; a source-supported sitting or lying pet rests naturally on the same floor. Never add any separate display base, round disk, circular slab, stand, plinth, pedestal, podium, raised presentation platform, mounting plate or support post, whether black, white, transparent or any other colour. The white studio floor has no separate hard-edged disk or slab underneath the subject(s). This prohibition concerns presentation supports only: preserve genuine source-owned footwear, including thick platform shoes, sole thickness, tread, shape and colour; never flatten, remove or recolour a shoe or its sole to obey this rule. Keep all existing source clothing, accessories, held items, markings and pose requirements. All existing rules for rich, varied and harmonious completion of genuinely unseen clothing remain in force.'

